    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d575-a4">

                <pb facs="1035" n="941" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg941"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No. 13.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Order for sale of schooner Eliza.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Yokohama</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-05-04"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 4,
                        1882</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>By order of H. I. Russian Majesty’s court at Kanagawa, was sold at public auction
                    on the 2d day of May, 1882, the schooner <hi rendition="#italic">Kiwa
                        Elizabeth</hi>, to foreclose a mortgage held by F; C. Spooner on said
                    vessel. The said vessel was sold to said Spooner for the sum of $3,600, the
                    acknowledgment of payment of said sum constituting a bill of sale for the said
                    schooner. N. 86.</p>
                <closer>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">seal.</hi>] <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >A. Pelikan</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">H. I. Majesty’s
                            Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
